From 7eae04af52fe9bed536e046b2522847d30cf3b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Glombek <c.glombek@cosa.systems>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 10:41:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [network-manager] do not re-register the ubus watch while
 shutting down

ThreadBorderRouterManagementCluster uses the delegate's Init() for two opposite
purposes: Startup() passes the attribute-change callback, and Shutdown() passes
nullptr to detach it. OpenThreadUbusBorderRouterDelegate treated both as a fresh
initialisation and registered its ubus watch either way.

That second call arrives on the way down. ChipLinuxAppMainLoop runs
ApplicationShutdown() before Server::Shutdown(), so by the time the cluster
detaches its callback the application has already stopped the UbusManager, and
UbusManager::Register() asserts that it is initialised. The daemon therefore
aborted on every clean shutdown:

  SPT: VerifyOrDie failure at UbusManager.cpp:163: mInitialized

Return early when there is no callback: detaching is not initialisation, and it
has nothing to register.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5
---
 .../network-manager-app/linux/ThreadBROpenThreadUbus.cpp   | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/examples/network-manager-app/linux/ThreadBROpenThreadUbus.cpp b/examples/network-manager-app/linux/ThreadBROpenThreadUbus.cpp
index 97ac76ca7b..6c11534b87 100644
--- a/examples/network-manager-app/linux/ThreadBROpenThreadUbus.cpp
+++ b/examples/network-manager-app/linux/ThreadBROpenThreadUbus.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,13 @@ CHIP_ERROR OpenThreadUbusBorderRouterDelegate::Init(AttributeChangeCallback * at
 {
     mAttributeChangeCallback = attributeChangeCallback;
 
+    // The cluster uses Init() for two opposite things: Startup() passes the
+    // callback, and Shutdown() passes nullptr to detach it. The second runs on
+    // the way down, by which point ApplicationShutdown() has already stopped
+    // the ubus manager -- and registering a watch on a stopped manager is a
+    // VerifyOrDie. Detaching is not a fresh initialisation, so stop here.
+    VerifyOrReturnValue(attributeChangeCallback != nullptr, CHIP_NO_ERROR);
+
     mOtbr.SetResolvedCallback([](UbusWatch & watch, void * appState) {
         auto * self = static_cast<decltype(this)>(appState);
         ubus_invoke(&self->mUbusManager.Context(), watch.ObjectID(), "status", nullptr,
